sequenceDiagram
    participant Operator as Operator / SRE
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Pod as Model Server Pod
    participant Preflight as Preflight Script<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant vLLM as vLLM Serve
    participant GPU as NVIDIA GPU

    Note over Pod,vLLM: Flow 1: Preflight Check Gating vLLM Startup

    Pod->>Preflight: Container command executes<br/>preflight-checks.py (process exec)
    Preflight->>GPU: nvidia-smi queries<br/>GPU topology, NVLink, PCIe
    GPU-->>Preflight: Topology diagnostics
    Preflight->>Preflight: Print diagnostics to stdout/stderr

    alt LLMD_PREFLIGHT_CHECKS=pause
        Preflight->>Preflight: Start HTTP server on port 8000
        K8s->>Preflight: GET /health (liveness probe)
        Preflight-->>K8s: 200 OK
        Operator->>Preflight: GET /info (inspect environment)
        Preflight-->>Operator: System diagnostics JSON
        Operator->>Preflight: GET /exit (release hold)
        Preflight-->>Operator: Shutting down
    end

    Preflight->>vLLM: Exit 0 → vLLM serve binds port 8000
    vLLM->>GPU: Allocate GPU memory

    Note over Operator,GPU: Flow 2: NIXL Benchmark Transfer

    participant Creator as Creator Agent<br/>benchmark.py
    participant ZMQ as ZMQ Socket<br/>5555/TCP
    participant Peer as Peer Agent<br/>benchmark.py
    participant PeerGPU as Peer GPU VRAM

    Creator->>GPU: Allocate PyTorch tensors on GPU
    Peer->>PeerGPU: Allocate PyTorch tensors on GPU
    Creator->>ZMQ: Send NIXL agent metadata
    ZMQ->>Peer: Receive metadata (ZMQ PAIR)
    Peer-->>ZMQ: Send peer metadata
    ZMQ-->>Creator: Receive peer metadata
    Creator->>PeerGPU: NIXL GPU VRAM-to-VRAM transfer<br/>UCX (RDMA/TCP, dynamic port)
    Peer->>Peer: Verify transferred data correctness

    Note over Operator,GPU: Flow 3: Networking Test Execution

    participant Runner as run-tests.py
    participant ServerPod as Server Pod
    participant ClientPod as Client Pod

    Operator->>Runner: Execute test suite
    Runner->>K8s: Discover pods by label<br/>kubectl (HTTPS/443, kubeconfig)
    K8s-->>Runner: Pod list
    Runner->>ServerPod: kubectl exec: start server<br/>(perftest/iperf3/nixlbench)
    Runner->>ClientPod: kubectl exec: start client
    ClientPod->>ServerPod: Test traffic<br/>(RDMA/TCP/UCX, various ports)
    ServerPod-->>ClientPod: Test results
    Runner->>Runner: Compare against baselines<br/>flag outliers
